ot;,&quot;style&quot;:{&quot;width&quot;:&quot;640px&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:&quot;829px&quot;,&quot;position&quot;:&quot;relative&quot;,&quot;backgroundPosition&quot;:&quot;0 0&quot;},&quot;data-bg&quot;:&quot;/api/v1/documents/unlocked/13635412/bg/8eb106def50fabd1460e37d4beb2604c/77.jpg&quot;,&quot;altHeight&quot;:null}"><div data-testid="ch-page-slice" class="ch-page-slice" data-page="77" style="width:630px;height:829px;position:relative;background-position:0 0;overflow:hidden"><span id="t1_77" class="t s1_77" data-oc="true">Relative Strength Index - 5th Grade: Common Chart Indicators - Beginne...</span><span id="t2_77" class="t s1_77" data-oc="true">http://www.babypips.com/school/relative_strength_index.html </span><span id="t3_77" class="t s1_77" data-oc="true">1 of 2</span><span id="t4_77" class="t s1_77" data-oc="true">11/13/2007 4:07 PM</span><span id="t5_77" class="t s2_77" data-oc="true">Relative Strength Index </span><span id="t6_77" class="t s3_77" data-oc="true">Print and run! Prefer to print out these lessons? </span><span id="t7_77" class="t s4_77" data-oc="true">Buy the PDF</span><span id="t8_77" class="t s3_77" data-oc="true">. Only $49. </span><span id="t9_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">Relative Strength Index, or RSI, is similar to stochastics in that it identifies </span><span id="ta_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">overbought and oversold conditions in the market. </span><span id="tb_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">It is also scaled from 0 to 100. </span><span id="tc_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">Typically, readings below 20 indicate oversold, while readings over 80 indicate </span><span id="td_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">overbought. </span><span id="te_77" class="t s6_77" data-oc="true">Using RSI </span><span id="tf_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">RSI can be used just like stochastics. </span><span id="tg_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">From the chart above you can see that when </span><span id="th_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">RSI dropped below 20, it correctly identified an oversold market. </span><span id="ti_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">After the drop, </span><span id="tj_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">the price quickly shot back up. </span><span id="tk_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">RSI is a very popular tool because it can also be used to confirm trend formations. </span><span id="tl_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">If you think a trend is forming, take a quick look at the RSI and look at whether it </span><span id="tm_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">is above or below 50. </span><span id="tn_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">If you are looking at a possible uptrend, then make sure the </span><span id="to_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">RSI is above 50. </span><span id="tp_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">If you are looking at a possible downtrend, then make sure the </span><span id="tq_77" class="t s5_77" data-oc="true">RSI is below 50. </span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-testid="page-container" class="page-container tw-relative" data-page="78"><div class="CYtV78FustZrAng5u4BPfw=="><div data-html-viewer-page="78" style="transform:scale(calc( var(--initial-viewer-width) / 640));transform-origin:top left"><div data-testid="html-preview-wrapper" style="height:calc(829px * var(--initial-viewer-width) / 640)"><div data-block="true" data-originaltag="{&quot;tagName&quot;:&quot;div&quot;,&quot;attribs&quot;:{&quot;data-height&quot;:&quot;829&quot;,&quot;data-width&quot;:&quot;640&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;html-prev-78&quot;}}" data-props="{&quot;dataHeight&quot;:&quot;829&quot;}"><div><div data-block="true" data-originaltag="{&quot;tagName&quot;:&quot;div&quot;,&quot;attribs&quot;:{&quot;class&quot;:&quot;html-preview-text&quot;}}" data-props="{&quot;className&quot;:&quot;html-preview-text&quot;,&quot;testId&quot;:&quot;html-preview-text&quot;}"><div class="html-preview-text" data-testid="html-preview-text">