 you need to know about the Elliott Wave Theory. Remember the </span><span id="td_127" class="t s2_127" data-oc="true">market moves in waves. Now when you hear somebody say "Wave 2 is complete." </span><span id="te_127" class="t s2_127" data-oc="true">You'll know what the heck he is talking about. </span><span id="tf_127" class="t s2_127" data-oc="true">If you wish to become an Elliott Wave Theory guru, you can learn more about it at </span><span id="tg_127" class="t s3_127" data-oc="true">www.elliottwave.com</span><span id="th_127" class="t s2_127" data-oc="true">. </span><span id="ti_127" class="t s4_127" data-oc="true">Â« Previous</span><span id="tj_127" class="t s4_127" data-oc="true">1</span><span id="tk_127" class="t s2_127" data-oc="true">2</span><span id="tl_127" class="t s3_127" data-oc="true">3</span><span id="tm_127" class="t s3_127" data-oc="true">Next Â» </span><span id="tn_127" class="t s5_127" data-oc="true">"Doing the best at this moment puts you in the best place for the next moment." </span><span id="to_127" class="t s5_127" data-oc="true">Oprah Winfrey </span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-testid="page-container" class="page-container tw-relative" data-page="128"><div class="CYtV78FustZrAng5u4BPfw=="><div data-html-viewer-page="128" style="transform:scale(calc( var(--initial-viewer-width) / 640));transform-origin:top left"><div data-testid="html-preview-wrapper" style="height:calc(829px * var(--initial-viewer-width) / 640)"><div data-block="true" data-originaltag="{&quot;tagName&quot;:&quot;div&quot;,&quot;attribs&quot;:{&quot;data-height&quot;:&quot;829&quot;,&quot;data-width&quot;:&quot;640&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;html-prev-128&quot;}}" data-props="{&quot;dataHeight&quot;:&quot;829&quot;}"><div><div data-block="true" data-originaltag="{&quot;tagName&quot;:&quot;div&quot;,&quot;attribs&quot;:{&quot;class&quot;:&quot;html-preview-text&quot;}}" data-props="{&quot;className&quot;:&quot;html-preview-text&quot